## openvela QuickApp Lifecycle

openvela (an open-source IoT operating system based on NuttX) supports QuickApps with the following lifecycle callbacks:

| Lifecycle Method | Description |
|---|---|
| **`onInit()`** | Called when the QuickApp page is first created/initialized. Used for setting up initial state. |
| **`onShow()`** | Called when the page becomes visible (foreground). Good place to start sensors, animations, etc. |
| **`onHide()`** | Called when the page goes to the background. Ideal for pausing/stopping sensors to save power. |
| **`onDestroy()`** | Called when the page is destroyed. Clean up all resources here. |

## Sensor Management Pattern

```javascript
// Typical pattern in openvela QuickApp
export default {
  onInit() {
    // Initialize sensor references
  },
  onShow() {
    // Start sensor listening
    this.sensorId = sensor.subscribeSensor('accelerometer', 100, (data) => {
      this.accelData = data;
    });
  },
  onHide() {
    // Stop sensor to conserve power
    sensor.unsubscribeSensor(this.sensorId);
  },
  onDestroy() {
    // Final cleanup
  }
};
```

